# Live severity via the Grafana MCP (`agatha-mcp`)

Confirm how bad it is with real numbers rather than only linking a dashboard.
Guard on availability. If the `agatha-mcp` tools are not connected, skip this and
link the standing dashboard.

## Principle: reuse curated panel queries

Do not hand-write PromQL. The standing dashboards hold the right recording-rule
query per signal. Pull the panel query and run it for the affected environment.

## Standing dashboards

{{DASHBOARDS}}

## Workflow

1. `grafana_get_dashboard_panel_queries(uid=<dashboard>)`. Returns panels with
   `title`, `query`, and `datasource` (often `${cloud}`).
2. Pick the panel whose **title matches the signal**. Error rate, latency, event
   loop lag, pod restarts, memory, LB 5xx.
3. `grafana_query_prometheus` with `datasourceUid` set to the environment cloud id
   (see Environments in `runbook-sources.md`). Instant for now. A short range for
   the trend.
4. Report the current value, whether it breaches the alert threshold, and roughly
   when it started. `grafana_get_panel_image` renders a snapshot.

## Guardrails

- If a query errors or returns no data, say so. Never invent a number.
- Keep ranges short. This runs during an incident.
- Match by panel title at runtime. Do not hardcode recording-rule names.
